<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">

    <uses-feature
        android:name="android.hardware.type.watch"
        android:required="true" />

    <!--
      No sensor or health permission is declared. See
      docs/reports/PHASE_4_PERMISSION_INVESTIGATION.md.

      ACTIVITY_RECOGNITION was removed because it backed no feature at all:
      the face spec and the generated WFF XML reference no step, activity,
      distance, calorie or floor source. It was declared and never used.

      BODY_SENSORS was removed because an unqualified declaration is wrong
      on an API-36-only package. Apps targeting API 36+ must declare the
      granular android.permission.health.* permissions instead; the legacy
      permission only applies with android:maxSdkVersion="35", and minSdk
      is 36, so it could never take effect
      (developer.android.com/training/wearables/versions/6/changes,
      checked 2026-07-26).

      Heart rate reaches this face only as the declarative WFF
      [HEART_RATE] source. The package has android:hasCode="false": it
      cannot call an API, cannot request a runtime permission, and cannot
      handle a permission result. The face also has a documented fallback
      (HEART_RATE < 30 -> 70 bpm), so an unavailable reading degrades into
      an already-tested state rather than breaking.

      This is the minimum declaration. Empirical confirmation on the
      Galaxy Watch7 that live HR still drives the balance wheel with no
      permission declared is a BLOCKED readiness gate, not a settled
      result. A controlled variant declaring
      android.permission.health.READ_HEART_RATE is built alongside the
      candidate for comparison if the device shows it is required.
    -->

    <application
        android:label="AURELIUS"
        android:icon="@drawable/preview"
        android:hasCode="false">

        <property
            android:name="com.google.wear.watchface.format.version"
            android:value="@integer/wff_version" />

        <meta-data
            android:name="com.google.android.wearable.standalone"
            android:value="true" />
    </application>
</manifest>
